  "live_records": {
    "q-65228": {
      "dom_id": "step-q65228",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "${cos}^{2}⁡x(\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+1)=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we expand the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡x(\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+1) & ={cos}^{2}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}+{cos}^{2}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+{cos}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x{sin}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}+\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+{cos}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\cancel{{cos}^{2}⁡x}}+\\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}+{cos}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & ={sin}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\  & =1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that, in the last step, we simplified the right-hand side using ${cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1.$ \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x(\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+1)=1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
