    "q-1578": {
      "dom_id": "step-q1578",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "$(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{2}+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{2}=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we expand the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{2}+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{2} & =({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\  & =({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x-\\cancel{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})+({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x+\\cancel{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}) \\\\  & ={sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =2{sin}^{2}⁡x+2{cos}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =2({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use ${sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x=1$ to simplify the expression in the parentheses. This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)=2\\cdot (1)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{2}+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{2}=2.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
