    "q-65193": {
      "dom_id": "step-q65193",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Simplify the trigonometric expression ${sin}^{2}⁡x{cos}^{3}⁡x+{sin}^{4}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we factor the expression:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡x{cos}^{3}⁡x+{sin}^{4}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x={sin}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot ({cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x)\n$$\n\nThen, we use ${cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1$ to simplify the expression in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot ({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x) & ={sin}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={sin}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that \n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡x{cos}^{3}⁡x+{sin}^{4}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x={sin}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
